Speech at controlled noise levels, with the reference implementation's output beside it.

    in_SNR5.wav    speech mixed with noise at 5 dB SNR
    out_SNR5.wav   what mmse_log_spu.py makes of it
    in_SNR15.wav   the same at 15 dB
    out_SNR15.wav

All of it is made here, by gen.py, and is this project's own. The speech is espeak-ng reading a few
requests; the noise is pink noise and a low hum from a fixed seed. The out_ files are the reference
implementation, mmse_log_spu.py from github.com/vipchengrui/traditional-speech-enhancement (MIT, which
follows Loizou, Speech Enhancement: Theory and Practice), fetched at a pinned commit and run as it is.
Mono, 16-bit, 8 kHz.

The denoiser has to be checked against that reference on the same input, which is why its output is
kept beside each input. python3 gen.py (Linux or WSL, with espeak-ng, numpy and scipy) makes all four
again.
